    "created_at": "2023-03-15T23:03:14Z",
    "updated_at": "2023-03-15T23:03:14Z",
    "body": "Oh, oof. I'd be hesitant to go for Chromium's behavior in that case. Having the base URL inheritance-or-not be determined by sandboxing seems reasonable. Having it determined by a mix of sandboxing and the precise flavor of about: URL, seems like just a weird special case.\r\n\r\nCan you say more about why Chromium thinks changing this behavior for sandboxed about:blank is a good idea? Otherwise I think aligning on the Firefox+Safari behavior is the best path here, as it gives a shorter path to interop and a simpler spec/implementation. Your OP says \"insecure\", but in what way? What is the threat model; who is attacking who, and what do they accomplish which would be changed by the special-casing?",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
